$$\mathcal{L}_{\text{EM}} = -\frac{1}{4} \exp\left( -2\alpha_0 \int \frac{\partial_\mu \Phi}{\sqrt{-\eta^{\alpha\beta} \partial_\alpha \Phi \partial_\beta \Phi}} dx^\mu \right) F_{\alpha\beta} F^{\alpha\beta}$$

Because every tensor index ($\mu, \alpha, \beta$) is fully contracted with the Minkowski metric $\eta_{\mu\nu}$, the fundamental action is 100% Lorentz invariant under any arbitrary Lorentz boost or spatial rotation.

